      "statement": "A graph claim stated at a cut reports a verdict only through the transfer rules: absence transfers exactly, a coarse path is a may-path unless a chain of relationships between members witnesses it, acyclicity is a statement about blocks; a claim naming an element hidden at its cut is not expressible at that level (I9).",
      "subjects": [
        "claim-evaluator",
        "semantic-abstraction"
      ],
      "evaluate": {
        "method": "external-evidence"
      }
